# SEO standards

The site is fully static Astro on GitHub Pages. Full architecture: `docs/SEO.md`.

## Single sources of truth
- Site URL, name, author, default description, default social image, profile URLs: `src/lib/seo-config.mjs`. Never hard-code them elsewhere.
- Head tags (title, description, canonical, robots, Open Graph, Twitter, JSON-LD): `src/components/Seo.astro`, rendered by `BaseLayout`. New pages use `BaseLayout`; do not add ad-hoc `<meta>` tags.
- JSON-LD builders: `src/lib/seo.ts`. Add new schema types there.

## Every public page must have
- A unique, accurate `title` and `description` (title ≲ 60 chars, description 70-160).
- A canonical URL (absolute, `https://jpurohit92.github.io/...`, trailing slash). Generated by `Seo.astro`; only override for content first published elsewhere.
- Open Graph and Twitter tags with an absolute image URL (default: `public/og-default.png`).
- Exactly one `<h1>`; headings never skip a level.

## Crawlable static HTML
- Content must be in the built HTML. No `client:only` for content, no content injected by JS.
- Internal links are real `<a href>` URLs with a trailing slash (`/blog/`, not `/blog`).
- Reading mode is CSS/JS state on the same URL. Never create separate reading-mode URLs.
- Do not change a published URL without a redirect (`redirects` in `astro.config.mjs`).

## Structured data
- JSON-LD must match visible content. Never invent values (no fake ratings, authors, profiles, dates).
- Omit optional fields that have no real value (e.g. `dateModified`, `image`).

## Sitemap and robots
- Keep `@astrojs/sitemap`. Drafts, `noindex` posts, canonical-elsewhere posts, redirects and 404 stay out (filter in `astro.config.mjs`).
- `robots.txt` is generated by `src/pages/robots.txt.ts` and must point to `/sitemap-index.xml`.

## Images
- Every `<img>` has `alt` (use `alt=""` only for decorative images) plus `width`/`height`.
- Use `astro:assets` (`<Image>`) for images in `src/`; above-the-fold images get `loading="eager"` and `fetchpriority="high"`.

## After any change to pages, layouts, components, content, config or public/
Run `npm run build && npm run seo:check`. Fix every error. Treat recommendations as editorial advice. Do not weaken `scripts/seo-check.mjs` to make it pass.
